    {
      "id": "crown-of-crows",
      "title": "Crown of Crows",
      "playstyle": "Hide durable Archer formations behind Guards, stack their Strength with completed Names, and punish attackers with delayed Archer responses.",
      "hypothesis": "Can a guarded Archer line convert its setup into a decisive Strength advantage without relying on surveillance or repeated relocation?",
      "combo_notes": [
        "Crow Archers + a Bond + Corin of the High Wall or Serai, Queen of Crows combines Empowered pressure, Archer classifications, and multiple +1 Strength effects; Every Bow Was Strung rewards bonded Archers.",
        "Old Guard in Middle protects a Rear Archer from basic Archer Attacks. Thornbow Hunters in Rear give every other friendly Archer in their Front +1 Strength; First Spear can Guard the Middle screen.",
        "The Archers Were Ready can trigger a free legal Archer Attack after an enemy Attack. The Crows Came Down now reduces opposing Strength by 1 when it Exhausts on PLAY and can add Shaken (−2) with a later ACTION; track whether this stacked −3 swing is too reliable.",
        "Serai + other Archers + The Battle Had Chosen Them pushes Strength, while Asha, Alda, Veyra, No Step Back and Guarded protect crucial formations from hostile effects."
      ],
