    {
      "id": "oathforge",
      "title": "Oathforge",
      "playstyle": "Build high-Strength Named Formations through Bond discounts, prepared layers and completion rewards, then protect the finished stacks.",
      "hypothesis": "Do the attachment chains create enough persistent Strength and defensive redundancy to justify setup Actions against ordinary Force deployment?",
      "combo_notes": [
        "Late Banner + Followed + a Name yields a cheaper Named stack with an extra Bond Strength bonus; The Battle Had Chosen Them rewards that same Named state.",
        "Tovan, the Quartermaster discounts Bonds and Names. Torren supplies immediate Bond attachment, while Oren discounts a Bond by 1 Command once per Battle and draws if it completes a Named formation. Namar restores Command and discounts another attachment.",
        "Field Train delivers a prepared layer from its Front or an adjacent active Front and grants +2 Strength if it completes Named. House of Reed can attach one prepared layer on PLAY and up to two more with one once-per-Battle ACTION, giving Guarded to formations completed. Stayed Behind For can send a prepared Name to another friendly Force.",
        "Teren turns Named completion into a free Stratagem setting Action; There Was No Road Back can then punish an enemy Bond or reposition a completed stack. Avaros and the Banner Stratagem convert prepared strength into a winning Front."
      ],
