    {
      "id": "blood-and-spoils",
      "title": "Blood & Spoils",
      "playstyle": "Combine persistent high-Strength Raiders with Archer Exhaustion, Skirmisher Shaken penalties, Command transfers and attachment raids.",
      "hypothesis": "Can Exhaustion and Shaken turn into genuine Strength and Command advantages without leaving the deck unable to defend or finish a Front?",
      "combo_notes": [
        "Crow Archers or The Baggage Was Abandoned Exhaust an enemy for −1 Strength. The Unnamed Host and Shared the Spoils With then turn that Exhaustion into Command advantage; Brannoc or Black Company can strip an attachment.",
        "Red Duelists and Tala apply Shaken (−2) to swing a contested Front. Iron Boars Deplete exposed support for −1 Strength and suppress ACTION abilities throughout that formation, enabling The Stores Were Taken to threaten a Bond.",
        "Raider or Skirmisher affliction can activate The Trap Closed, returning an attached Bond/Name; All Reserves Forward and Seized the Standard of offer additional layer removal instead of relying on movement.",
        "Rovan, Doros and Red Shields provide durable raw Strength, while Serai + Crow Archers + The Archers Were Ready gives an independent defensive counterattack and Strength line."
      ],
